messages:
maria_cs: Hey @jordan_dev — NovusMobile is onboarding and seeing a ton of 429s from our preflight endpoint during Android SDK init. They report spikes right after app launch. Pasting condensed logs below. Any quick mitigation we can suggest to keep them healthy while we dig in?

novus_ops: logs: 
`POST /v1/preflight 429` x20 within 30s, all from same client IP. Using Android SDK 0.9.7. Token refreshs look frequent, ephemeral TTL 60s.

jordan_dev: thanks — likely a preflight fanout + ephemeral token window. Two quick questions: are they calling init on every Activity start? and are they using the browser/webview path or direct native?

novus_ops: we call SDK.init() on each cold Activity (legacy code). Native.

sara_engineer: yep that's the pattern. Android cold starts + calling init everywhere + short ephemeral TTL = stampede. Recommend: 1) coalesce init calls (single shared Application init), 2) bump ephemeral TTL if possible, 3) client-side jitter/backoff on preflight, 4) use connection reuse/http2 keepalive.

maria_cs: can we give them a small code snippet to patch quickly? Novus wants a quick workaround before we schedule a deeper call.

jordan_dev: share this snippet for Application-level init and a token cache: 
```java
public class MyApp extends Application {
  @Override public void onCreate() {
    super.onCreate();
    SDK.init(getApplicationContext(), new SDKConfig.Builder()
      .setPreflightCache(true) // local short-lived cache
      .setEphemeralTtlSeconds(120) // bump to 2m if allowed
      .build());
  }
}

// naive token cache example
AtomicReference<String> cachedToken = new AtomicReference<>();
String getToken() {
  String t = cachedToken.get();
  if (t == null || isExpiringSoon(t)) {
    synchronized(this) {
      if (cachedToken.get() == null || isExpiringSoon(cachedToken.get())) {
        cachedToken.set(fetchNewToken());
      }
    }
  }
  return cachedToken.get();
}
```

sara_engineer: also recommend client backoff for 429s: exponential with jitter, and a local circuit-breaker after N rapid 429s to avoid repeated fanout. Example: start with 200ms, *2, jitter up to 100ms, cap 5s.

maria_cs: copied. Novus asked if server-side we can do anything short-term (before we tune preflight routing).

jordan_dev: on our end we can enable preflight coalescing for that tenant (group similar inits into a single upstream preflight) and temporarily raise their quota window to smooth the ramp. I'll request ops to apply a tenant-level preflight-coalesce flag.

deploy-bot: Request 87321 created: "tenant-coalesce: novusmobile" — assigned to eng-infra. ETA ~2h.

novus_ops: that sounds great. We'll push quick patch to Application-level init and token cache now. Any log patterns we should watch?

sara_engineer: watch rate of `POST /v1/preflight` per client token and per ip, and watch `token_age_seconds` headers (if SDK surfaces). Look for repeated token refresh within <TTL/2. Also check for many concurrent connections showing same user-agent — that indicates fanout.

maria_cs: I'll send the patch snippet + suggested backoff + note that ops has temporary coalesce request in flight. Thanks team. Will follow up after Novus deploys the patch. :thumbsup:
